<title>GERMANY: DBKom sees 7 bln dm sales in Germany by 2005.</title>
<headline>DBKom sees 7 bln dm sales in Germany by 2005.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications newcomer DBKom GmbH expects to have sales of up to seven billion marks by the year 2005, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>DBKom is owned by a consortium that includes the German railway Deutsche Bahn AG, Mannesmann AG, AT&amp;T Corp, and Unisource NV.</p>
<p>Speaking to a conference of business executives, Peter Bross, a Mannesmann executive, said two-thirds of DBKom sales would come from voice telephone services with the rest coming from data and value-added services.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
